    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1429">

                <pb facs="1209" n="1105" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1105"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.55/2.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 15, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A bill has been presented to the Legislature modifying the laws relating to
                    prohibition of immigration of Chinese, Turks, Syrians <pb facs="1210" n="1106"
                        xml:id="pg1106"/> and North Africans, but authorizing entry of Chinese under
                    contract. Immigration is prohibited by this bill notwithstanding naturalization
                    in another country. Severe restrictions and heavy licenses are imposed on
                    associations of the foreigners mentioned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodge</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
